      "Language": "spa",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A 56 year old man with fever and lumbar pain who underwent an abdominal CT scan that showed lumbar arthrosic changes, although it was not possible to rule out infectious disease in L5/S1. Bone scintigraphy was requested. It showed heterogeneous hyperuptake that did not make it possible to exclude a spondylodiscitis in this site. Scintigraphy with 67Ga-citrate excluded infectious diseases in the lumbar spine column. However, a pathological uptake was observed in the left iliac fossa suggestive of psoas abscess, which was confirmed by ultrasonography, isolating streptococcus viridans."},
